IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Composition of Offences) Regulations 2005 (S 706/2005), made under section 64 of the
-- Act (section 84 in the 2020 Revised Edition), in force 11 November 2005, and its amendment S 686/2011 (28 December
-- 2011).  Both are deposited in
-- subjects/sg/telecommunications-composition-of-offences-regulations-2005/registers/source-bundle/
-- (TA1999-COMP-S706-2005, TA1999-COMP-S686-2011).  The offences are named by their 2000 Revised Edition numbers: s 33 is
-- today's s 53, s 34 is s 54 and s 35 is s 55 (see sgta-part6-offences.l4).  Before 15 October 2001 -> NOTHING (the 2000 Regulations, S 260/2000, which S 516/2001 reg 3 revokes, are not deposited); from 15 October 2001 to
-- 10 November 2005 the 2001 Regulations, S 516/2001 (the "Rg 2" that reg 3 of the 2005 Regulations revokes), apply: see the last section.

§ `Composition of Offences Regulations 2005: citation, compoundable offences, revocation`

-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:17 | In exercise of the powers conferred by section 64 of the Telecommunications Act,
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:18 | the Info-communications Development Authority of Singapore, with the approval of the
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:19 | Minister for Information, Communications and the Arts, hereby makes the following
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:20 | Regulations:
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:22 | Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:23 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Composition of
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:24 | Offences) Regulations 2005 and shall come into operation on 11th November 2005.
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:26 | Compoundable offences
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:27 | 2. The following offences may be compounded by the Authority in accordance with
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:28 | section 64 (1) of the Act:
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:29 | (a) any offence under section 21 (7), 26 (8), 29 (6) or (9), 31 (1), 32, 32E (3), 33
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:30 | (1), (3) or (4), 34 (2), 35 (1) or (3), 39, 40 (1), 45, 46, 48, 49 (1), (2) or (3), 52 or
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:31 | 59 (6) of the Act;
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:32 | (b) any offence under the Telecommunications (Certificates of Competency for
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:33 | Ship Station Operators) Regulations (Rg 1);
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:34 | (c) any offence under the Telecommunications (Cable Detection Workers)
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:35 | Regulations (Rg 4);
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:36 | (d) any offence under the Telecommunications (Radio-communication)
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:37 | Regulations (Rg 5);
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:38 | (e) any offence under the Telecommunications (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 6); and
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:39 | (f) any offence under the Telecommunications (Internal Wiring) Regulations 2005
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:40 | (G.N. No. S 479/2005).
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:41 | Revocation
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:42 | 3. The Telecommunications (Composition of Offences) Regulations (Rg 2) are revoked.
@ref Comp Regs 2005 enacting words, regs 1 to 3 (src:TA1999-COMP-S706-2005:17-42)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Comp Regs reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date (from 11 November 2005)` MEANS
    d AT LEAST (Date 11 11 2005)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Comp Regs reg 3: the Telecommunications (Composition of Offences) Regulations (Rg 2) are revoked on the date` MEANS
    d AT LEAST (Date 11 11 2005)

GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Comp Regs reg 2(a): the sections of the Act (2000 Edition numbers) whose offences may be compounded` MEANS
    LIST "21(7)", "26(8)", "29(6)", "29(9)", "31(1)", "32", "32E(3)", "33(1)", "33(3)", "33(4)", "34(2)", "35(1)", "35(3)", "39", "40(1)", "45", "46", "48", "49(1)", "49(2)", "49(3)", "52", "59(6)"

GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Comp Regs reg 2(b) to (f), 2005 form: the subsidiary instruments whose offences may be compounded` MEANS
    LIST "Rg 1 Certificates of Competency for Ship Station Operators"
       , "Rg 4 Cable Detection Workers"
       , "Rg 5 Radio-communication"
       , "Rg 6 Dealers"
       , "Internal Wiring Regulations 2005"

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `section of the Act, by its 2000 Edition number` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Comp Regs reg 2(a): the offence under this section of the Act may be compounded` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 11 11 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (elem `section of the Act, by its 2000 Edition number` (`Comp Regs reg 2(a): the sections of the Act (2000 Edition numbers) whose offences may be compounded`))

-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:16 | In exercise of the powers conferred by section 64 of the
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:17 | Telecommunications Act, the Info-communications Development
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:18 | Authority of Singapore, with the approval of the Minister for
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:19 | Information, Communications and the Arts, hereby makes the
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:20 | following Regulations:
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:22 | Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:23 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:24 | (Composition of Offences) (Amendment) Regulations 2011 and shall
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:25 | come into operation on 28th December 2011.
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:27 | Amendment of regulation 2
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:28 | 2. Regulation 2 of the Telecommunications (Composition of
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:29 | Offences) Regulations 2005 (G.N. No. S 706/2005) is amended —
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:30 | (a) by deleting the word ‘‘and’’ at the end of paragraph (e); and
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:31 | (b) by deleting the full-stop at the end of paragraph (f) and
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:32 | substituting the word ‘‘; and’’, and by inserting immediately
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:33 | thereafter the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:34 | ‘‘(g) any offence under the Telecommunications (Class
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:35 | Licences) Regulations (Rg 3).’’.
@ref Comp Regs as amended by S 686/2011 (src:TA1999-COMP-S686-2011:16-35)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Comp Regs reg 2: the subsidiary instruments whose offences may be compounded, from 28 December 2011` MEANS
    append `Comp Regs reg 2(b) to (f), 2005 form: the subsidiary instruments whose offences may be compounded` (LIST "Rg 3 Class Licences")

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Comp Regs S 686/2011 reg 1: the amendment is in operation on the date (from 28 December 2011)` MEANS
    d AT LEAST (Date 28 12 2011)

-- S 560/2024, Telecommunications (Composition of Offences) (Amendment) Regulations 2024 (deposited 2026-11-04 from the e-Gazette's follow-up list): made 26 Jun 2024, FIRST PUBLISHED 28 Jun 2024 at 5 pm, in operation 1 Jul 2024.
-- Paragraph (f) of reg 2 (the Internal Wiring Regulations 2005) now reads "... as in force before 1 July 2024;", and a new paragraph (h) adds "any offence under regulation 6 of the Telecommunications (Wiring Work) Regulations 2024 (G.N. No. S 559/2024)",
-- which is the false-or-misleading-information offence (reg 6 of S 559/2024), not the wiring-work authorisation.  The reading day is not modelled for this instrument: it was published three days before it is in operation, so a reader on 28 to 30 June 2024
-- sees it for conduct on or after 1 July 2024 only, and a reader before 28 June 2024 does not see it at all.
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:14 | In exercise of the powers conferred by section 84(2) of the
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:15 | Telecommunications Act 1999, the Info‑communications Media
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:16 | Development Authority, with the approval of the Minister for
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:17 | Communications and Information, makes the following Regulations:
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:19 | Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:20 | 1. These Regulations are the Telecommunications (Composition of
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:21 | Offences) (Amendment) Regulations 2024 and come into operation
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:22 | on 1 July 2024.
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:24 | Amendment of regulation 2
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:25 | 2. In the Telecommunications (Composition of Offences)
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:26 | Regulations 2005 (G.N. No. S 706/2005), in regulation 2 —
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:27 | (a) in paragraph (f), replace “; and” at the end with “as in force
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:28 | before 1 July 2024;”;
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:29 | (b) in paragraph (g), replace the full‑stop at the end with
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:30 | “; and”; and
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:31 | (c) after paragraph (g), insert —
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:32 | “(h) any offence under regulation 6 of the
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:33 | Telecommunications (Wiring Work)
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:34 | Regulations 2024 (G.N. No. S 559/2024).”.
@ref Comp Regs as amended by S 560/2024 (1 July 2024) (src:TA1999-COMP-S560-2024:14-34)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Comp Regs reg 2: the subsidiary instruments whose offences may be compounded, from 1 July 2024` MEANS
    LIST "Rg 1 Certificates of Competency for Ship Station Operators"
       , "Rg 4 Cable Detection Workers"
       , "Rg 5 Radio-communication"
       , "Rg 6 Dealers"
       , "Internal Wiring Regulations 2005 as in force before 1 July 2024"
       , "Rg 3 Class Licences"
       , "Wiring Work Regulations 2024 regulation 6"

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Comp Regs S 560/2024 reg 1: the amendment is in operation on the date (from 1 July 2024)` MEANS
    d AT LEAST (Date 1 7 2024)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      instrument IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Comp Regs reg 2(b) to (h): the offences under this subsidiary instrument may be compounded on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 11 11 2005) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 28 12 2011) THEN JUST (elem instrument (`Comp Regs reg 2(b) to (f), 2005 form: the subsidiary instruments whose offences may be compounded`))
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2024) THEN JUST (elem instrument (`Comp Regs reg 2: the subsidiary instruments whose offences may be compounded, from 28 December 2011`))
           OTHERWISE JUST (elem instrument (`Comp Regs reg 2: the subsidiary instruments whose offences may be compounded, from 1 July 2024`))

-- The name this function had until S 560/2024 added paragraph (h); the answer for a date before 1 July 2024 is the same.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      instrument IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Comp Regs reg 2(b) to (g): the offences under this subsidiary instrument may be compounded on the date` MEANS
    `Comp Regs reg 2(b) to (h): the offences under this subsidiary instrument may be compounded on the date` d instrument

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- S 516/2001, the Telecommunications (Composition of Offences) Regulations 2001 (first published and in operation 15 October 2001; deposited 2026-11-04 from the e-Gazette's third list):
-- the Regulations as made, which the 2005 Regulations revoke (the "Rg 2" of the lines above).  Its reg 3 revokes the Composition Regulations 2000 (G.N. No. S 260/2000), which is NOT deposited,
-- so before 15 October 2001 the answer is NOTHING.  Its reg 2(a) names the sections of the Act by their 2000 Edition numbers; its reg 2(b) to (e) name particular regulations of the
-- Radio-communication Regulations 2001 (S 114/2001) and of the Dealers (Rg 7) and Internal Wiring (Rg 9) and Cable Detection Workers (S 196/2000) regulations, not the instruments as wholes.
-- The cap on a composition was $1,000 until Act 10 of 2005 raised it to $5,000 (s 64(1) of the 2000 Edition; the cap is encoded for the 2020 text in sgta-part8-penalties.l4, `s 84(1): the offence may be compounded for this sum`, and is not dated by version).
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:24 | In exercise of the powers conferred by section 64 of the
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:25 | Telecommunications Act, the Info-communications Development
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:26 | Authority of Singapore, with the approval of the Minister for
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:27 | Communications and Information Technology, hereby makes the
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:28 | following Regulations:
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:30 | Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:31 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:32 | (Composition of Offences) Regulations 2001 and shall come into
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:33 | operation on 15th October 2001.
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:35 | Compoundable offences
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:36 | 2. The following offences may be compounded by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:37 | in accordance with section 64 (1) of the Act:
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:38 | (a) sections 29 (1) and (3), 31 (1), 32, 33 (1), (3) and (4), 34 (2),
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:39 | 35 (1) and (3), 39, 40 (1), 45, 48, 49 (1), (2) and (3) and 52 of
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:40 | the Act;
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:41 | (b) regulations 24, 31, 32, 33, 35 (2), 36, 54, 56 (2), 57, 63 (1), (2)
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:42 | and (3), 64, 67, 68, 69 and 70 (read with regulation 78) of the
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:43 | Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:44 | 2001 (G. N. No. S 114/2001);
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:47 | (c) regulations 4 (1) and (4), 6 (2), 12 (2), 14, 15, 17, 18, 19,
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:48 | 20 (3) and (4) (read with regulation 32) of the Telecommu-
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:49 | nication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7);
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:50 | (d) any provision (read with regulation 16) of the Telecommu-
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:51 | nication (Internal Wiring) Regulations (Rg 9); and
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:52 | (e) regulations 8 (b), (c), (d) and (e) and 12 (read with
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:53 | regulation 14) of the Telecommunications (Cable Detection
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:54 | Workers) Regulations 2000 (G.N. No. S 196/2000).
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:56 | Revocation
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:57 | 3. The Telecommunications (Composition of Offences)
-- src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:58 | Regulations 2000 (G.N. No. S 260/2000) are revoked.
@ref Comp Regs 2001, S 516/2001 regs 1 to 3 (src:TA1999-COMP-S516-2001:24-58)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Comp Regs 2001 reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date (from 15 October 2001, until revoked on 11 November 2005)` MEANS
    (d AT LEAST (Date 15 10 2001)) AND (d LESS THAN (Date 11 11 2005))

GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Comp Regs 2001 reg 2(a): the sections of the Act (2000 Edition numbers) whose offences may be compounded` MEANS
    LIST "29(1)", "29(3)", "31(1)", "32", "33(1)", "33(3)", "33(4)", "34(2)", "35(1)", "35(3)", "39", "40(1)", "45", "48", "49(1)", "49(2)", "49(3)", "52"

GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Comp Regs 2001 reg 2(b): the regulations of the Radio-communication Regulations 2001 (S 114/2001) whose breach may be compounded` MEANS
    LIST "24", "31", "32", "33", "35(2)", "36", "54", "56(2)", "57", "63(1)", "63(2)", "63(3)", "64", "67", "68", "69", "70"

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `section of the Act, by its 2000 Edition number` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Comp Regs 2001 reg 2(a): the offence under this section of the Act may be compounded on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 15 10 2001) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 11 11 2005) THEN JUST (elem `section of the Act, by its 2000 Edition number` (`Comp Regs 2001 reg 2(a): the sections of the Act (2000 Edition numbers) whose offences may be compounded`))
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      regulation IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Comp Regs 2001 reg 2(b): the breach of this regulation of the Radio-communication Regulations may be compounded on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 15 10 2001) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 11 11 2005) THEN JUST (elem regulation (`Comp Regs 2001 reg 2(b): the regulations of the Radio-communication Regulations 2001 (S 114/2001) whose breach may be compounded`))
           OTHERWISE NOTHING
